{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cat clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c18-schema.json'","aggregated_output":"{\n \"type\": \"object\",\n \"additionalProperties\": false,\n \"required\": [\n  \"new_theses\",\n  \"evidence\"\n ],\n \"properties\": {\n  \"new_theses\": {\n   \"type\": \"array\",\n   \"description\": \"New thesis proposals, each referenced by at least one evidence link.\",\n   \"items\": {\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"additionalProperties\": false,\n    \"required\": [\n     \"local_id\",\n     \"description\",\n     \"outcome\",\n     \"period\",\n     \"opens_as\",\n     \"settled_by\",\n     \"closest_open_thesis\",\n     \"why_a_separate_bet\"\n    ],\n    \"properties\": {\n     \"local_id\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"Local reference for this new thesis in the answer; not a database ID.\"\n     },\n     \"description\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"The proposed research question, stated clearly.\"\n     },\n     \"outcome\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"The outcome or event being tracked by this thesis.\"\n     },\n     \"period\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n       {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"type\": \"null\"\n       }\n      ],\n      \"description\": \"The period or check date that settles the thesis: the one the item supports, or the one its reason fixes (section 3), with how it was set.\"\n     },\n     \"opens_as\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"enum\": [\n       \"product_node\",\n       \"binding_obligation\",\n       \"shared_quantity\",\n       \"policy_stage\"\n      ],\n      \"description\": \"The reason this thesis opens, one of the four in section 3.\"\n     },\n     \"settled_by\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"The public material that will settle the answer on a date (a filing, an official decision, a shipment confirmation, a statistics release).\",\n      \"pattern\": \"\\\\S\"\n     },\n     \"closest_open_thesis\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n       {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"type\": \"null\"\n       }\n      ],\n      \"description\": \"Exact ID of the open thesis closest to this one; null when the open list is empty.\"\n     },\n     \"why_a_separate_bet\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"Why an analyst would bet on this question separately from the closest open thesis: how their answers can move apart.\"\n     }\n    }\n   }\n  },\n  \"evidence\": {\n   \"type\": \"array\",\n   \"description\": \"Evidence statements extracted from this item, with their thesis links.\",\n   \"items\": {\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"additionalProperties\": false,\n    \"required\": [\n     \"local_id\",\n     \"summary\",\n     \"source_passages\",\n     \"original_party\",\n     \"reporting_speaker\",\n     \"tier\",\n     \"statement_date\",\n     \"statement_date_text\",\n     \"evidence_period\",\n     \"links\",\n     \"figures\"\n    ],\n    \"properties\": {\n     \"local_id\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"Local reference for this evidence in the answer; not a database ID.\"\n     },\n     \"summary\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"Standalone faithful summary naming the actor and preserving relevant figures, periods and conditions.\"\n     },\n     \"source_passages\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"minItems\": 1,\n      \"description\": \"Contiguous verbatim passages from this source item that jointly support the summary; return each passage separately.\",\n      \"items\": {\n       \"type\": \"string\"\n      }\n     },\n     \"original_party\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n       {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"type\": \"null\"\n       }\n      ],\n      \"description\": \"Party whose action, figure or claim is reported; null if unknown. Use the reporting outlet or author as the original party only for its own estimate, analysis or unnamed-source report.\"\n     },\n     \"reporting_speaker\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n       {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"type\": \"null\"\n       }\n      ],\n      \"description\": \"Person or outlet making or reporting the statement in this item, when known; null if unknown.\"\n     },\n     \"statement_date\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n       {\n        \"type\": \"string\",\n        \"pattern\": \"^[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}$\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"type\": \"null\"\n       }\n      ],\n      \"description\": \"Original statement day as YYYY-MM-DD when known; null if the full day is unknown.\"\n     },\n     \"figures\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n       \"type\": \"object\",\n       \"additionalProperties\": false,\n       \"required\": [\n        \"measure\",\n        \"period\",\n        \"value\",\n        \"kind\",\n        \"basis\"\n       ],\n       \"properties\": {\n        \"measure\": {\n         \"type\": \"string\",\n         \"description\": \"The financial measure as the passage states it.\"\n        },\n        \"period\": {\n         \"anyOf\": [\n          {\n           \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          {\n           \"type\": \"null\"\n          }\n         ],\n         \"description\": \"The period as stated; null when none is given.\"\n        },\n        \"value\": {\n         \"type\": \"string\",\n         \"description\": \"The figure copied exactly from one of this item's passages, with its unit.\"\n        },\n        \"kind\": {\n         \"type\": \"string\",\n         \"enum\": [\n          \"actual\",\n          \"guidance\",\n          \"estimate\"\n         ],\n         \"description\": \"actual: reported, including a balance as of a date; guidance: the company's own outlook; estimate: a named party's or consensus forecast.\"\n        },\n        \"basis\": {\n         \"anyOf\": [\n          {\n           \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          {\n           \"type\": \"null\"\n          }\n         ],\n         \"description\": \"Scope and qualifications as stated (GAAP or non-GAAP, segment or company, conditions); null when none.\"\n        }\n       }\n      },\n      \"description\": \"The company's own useful financial figures this statement states (section 2, CONDITION); empty for any other statement. A statement with several useful figures stays one item and lists them all.\"\n     },\n     \"links\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"minItems\": 0,\n      \"description\": \"The existing or proposed theses this evidence informs; empty when it is material but no thesis takes it yet: it is kept in the company's record and linked when a covering thesis opens.\",\n      \"items\": {\n       \"type\": \"object\",\n       \"additionalProperties\": false,\n       \"required\": [\n        \"target_type\",\n        \"target_id\",\n        \"relevance\"\n       ],\n       \"properties\": {\n        \"target_type\": {\n         \"type\": \"string\",\n         \"enum\": [\n          \"existing\",\n          \"new\"\n         ],\n         \"description\": \"Whether the reference identifies an open thesis or a new proposal.\"\n        },\n        \"target_id\": {\n         \"type\": \"string\",\n         \"description\": \"Exact supplied ID when existing, or local_id of a new thesis in this answer.\"\n        },\n        \"relevance\": {\n         \"type\": \"string\",\n         \"description\": \"How this evidence informs the referenced thesis, distinguishing source claims from inference.\"\n        }\n       }\n      }\n     },\n     \"tier\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"enum\": [\n       \"fact\",\n       \"party_statement\",\n       \"third_party_view\",\n       \"rumour\"\n      ],\n      \"description\": \"Source tier of the statement; an unconfirmed or unnamed-source claim takes precedence as rumour.\"\n     },\n     \"statement_date_text\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n       {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"type\": \"null\"\n       }\n      ],\n      \"description\": \"Original date or partial date as stated in the item; null when absent.\"\n     },\n     \"evidence_period\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n       {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"type\": \"null\"\n       }\n      ],\n      \"description\": \"Period the fact, plan or forecast describes, as supported by the item; null when unknown.\"\n     }\n    }\n   }\n  }\n }\n}","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cat clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c18-closing.txt'","aggregated_output":"Before you return the answer, check it once. Read each evidence item back as the analyst following the company and keep it when you would write it in this week's notes because it makes some question's answer more or less likely, about the company or its customers, suppliers, competitors, regulators or the economy. Ask first whether it is new: repeated common knowledge, a long-standing situation retold and an unargued view are noise. Do not drop a reported step, figure, guidance, forecast or decision because the item retells it or another outlet reported it before: a later step compares each statement with the evidence already stored and records a repeat there. Guidance, a forecast, a plan or a decision still in force keeps its place even when retold, including a change to a plan, design or schedule that another outlet reported days or weeks before. Judge the action or information itself, not its verb tense, and do not take a statement as old because its date is missing. Fitting one of the four kinds does not keep an item. A missing amount, date or scale never drops an item on its own: a forecast, a rumour, a counter-example or a distant or conditional statement is judged like any other.\nThese are not kept, even when a named party states them. What a row says it does not cover goes back to the test above, unless the row says it is kept:\n- background the analyst already knew, such as the company's history (\"the company was founded in 1998\"); an arrangement the item only describes as in place, even when no date is given: customers or partners that use, host, run or have built on the company's products, and the benefits they describe from that use (\"two airlines fly the planemaker's jets\"; \"three insurers run claims on the company's software and report faster payouts\"); a partnership, contract, plant or investment the item itself dates to an earlier month or year with no new step (\"earlier this year the company partnered with the glassmaker on three plants\"; \"in May it signed a $3 billion cloud contract\"); it does not cover a step the item reports as news, taken, decided, planned or under way (an order, a selection, an integration, an expansion, a deployment), even when it gives no date (\"the retailer's largest supplier is opening its own stores, people familiar said this week\"; \"the two largest cement makers are adding kilns to meet demand\"), nor a customer's, supplier's or partner's newly disclosed revenue, capacity, orders or contracted amount; a deal the item mentions as already existing is an arrangement in place even with its amount (\"a rival airline already leases 40 of the same jets\");\n- a typical claim that is common knowledge, without a figure and a specific account: that a firm leads or competes, that demand is strong or supply tight, a general risk (\"if demand slows it would hurt\"); a number does not lift a familiar position (\"the rival grocer has led this market for years and still holds 40%\"); it does not cover a dated forecast of a shortage, a price or demand (\"the steelmaker expects the shortage to peak next year and last until 2028\"), a competitor's newly reported share, volume or price in the company's market (\"the local rival now holds about half of the regional market, worth about $5 billion\"), nor a reported movement of a named price, rental rate, lead time or order book, even without a figure (\"rental rates for used trucks have been climbing this quarter\"); a general statement that demand stays strong or a product stays popular is not one;\n- a product, game, driver or benchmark specification with no business scale (\"the vacuum runs 60 minutes on a charge\"; \"a benchmark score\"), a retail price detail (\"a retailer marks one model down by $50\"), and a comparison the company, a partner or a third party publishes (\"the maker says its drug works twice as fast as older ones\"; \"a reviewer's test\"); it does not cover a competitor's comparison against the company's product, a partner's or customer's adoption or integration (also when a comparison shares its sentence), a reported launch, shipment, delay or cancellation of any of the company's products or a change to a product plan or configuration, including a reported sign that a planned product is going ahead (\"the long-range version of the jet is likely delayed or limited to a few deliveries\"; \"a parts supplier's catalogue lists the unannounced model\"), nor the company's decision to change the price it charges; uncertainty or a smaller product line does not make it a specification;\n- an unargued view or a quote that only characterises (\"the stock is a hold\"; \"a pivotal moment\"; \"an industry-leading platform\"), and a named analyst's reading of an event already recorded that adds no new fact or calculation (\"the recall shows quality risks are rising\"); it does not cover a reading that adds a new fact or calculation, nor the company's own statement that its plan, schedule or guidance still stands (\"the carmaker said the launch date has not moved\"), which is judged as the plan itself would be; a target price or valuation of the company is not kept, even with its assumptions and derivation, while the estimates it rests on are judged on their own (an analysts' earnings forecast is kept);\n- a political or strategic stance with no figure and no decision (\"diversifying suppliers will not reduce dependence\"); it does not cover a policy or regulatory step, nor a decision still in force that the item reports;\n- a share-price move, an investor's position or trade, or the market value (\"shares fell 13% this month\"; \"he is short the stock\"); it does not cover the news behind the move;\n- another company's matter that touches none of the company's markets (its valuation, share price, governance or a deal outside them), or that sits next to the company only by sharing an article, an event or an ecosystem; you supply the connection as the analyst and the item need not state it: a customer's spending, orders or backlog bears on demand, a supplier's capacity, output, prices or revenue on supply and input costs, a rival's products, prices or share in the company's markets on competition (\"a large customer's order backlog doubled\"; \"the main supplier's quarterly revenue jumped on demand for the part\");\n- the same fact said again in other words within this item: one deal, hire, programme or reported measure told in several sentences, with its terms, figures and growth rates, is one evidence item; keep the fuller wording (\"a $2 billion order for 120 stores in 15 countries over three years\"; \"cloud revenue of $8 billion, up 30% on the year and 6% on the quarter, 40% of the total\"); a deal one party signs under a wider programme, with its own amount or capacity, is its own evidence item, and a fact another outlet reported before is not a repeat within this item;\n- company boilerplate, bylines, forward-looking-statement text.\nA report and another party's denial or confirmation of it are two items, each kept only if it passes the test above; an estimate stays apart from any valuation drawn from it, and the valuation is not kept; one party's statement keeps its own planned or rumoured details.\nReturn only the evidence items you keep.\nThen check the theses and links. A new thesis that asks the same underlying question, about the same subject and scope, as an open thesis or another new thesis is not proposed: link its evidence to that thesis. A new thesis needs at least one kept evidence item, and a vague or noisy topic with no outcome to watch is not proposed. Each kept evidence item links to every thesis it informs and to no thesis its own relevance says it does not inform.\nFor each new thesis, check its opens_as, settled_by, closest_open_thesis and why_a_separate_bet: drop the thesis if it fits none of the four reasons in section 3, if no public material will settle it on a date, if an open thesis exists and its answer cannot move apart from it, or if it falls under a 'do not open' item in section 3; then link its evidence to every open thesis it informs, or leave it without links.\nAn item whose only home would be a new thesis that is not a big matter is returned with empty links and kept without links; an item an open thesis covers is linked there, not left without links. Then read back each statement you return with empty links that states the company's own figures: return it only if a figure can change what an analyst expects of the company's revenue, profitability, funding or credit risk, or competitive position; for example, a cash-rich company's balance or cash flow that the item ties to nothing usually cannot; return only what passes.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '4172,4203p' docs/DECISIONS-log.md\"","aggregated_output":"## D388 · 2026-11-09 · A material unsigned obligation gets its own signing question beside an open total of its kind\n\n- Asked: \"一笔重大的、还没签的承诺（比如为 OpenAI 俄亥俄数据中心租约做担保），要不要在已有的'担保总额'问题之外，单独开一个'会不会签'的问题？\"\n  Alex chose \"单独开 (Recommended)\".\n- **Decided.** A material unsigned obligation that merits a separate investment judgment keeps its own yes/no question on whether\n  it is signed by the check date, beside an open question on the total of the same kind. This confirms D248 boundary 1's exception,\n  which had not been put to him. A small unsigned obligation, or a deal already signed under a plan tracked by amount, stays evidence\n  for the total.\n- **Why it matters now.** The c8 dev draws fold the Ohio guarantee into the aggregate in 3 of 3, and q23 of the frozen judgement gold\n  asks it. Arm c9 showed that a sentence-level rule flips by send (round log §§48–50).\n- **Next.** A structural lever, designed and reviewed by the council before any send. c8 stays in force until a version is shown to\n  be better on new, unused articles.\n\n## D389 · 2026-11-09 · An unsigned obligation is large enough for its own signing question at about 5% of the company's annual profit\n\n- Asked: \"“多大算大”用什么尺寸？\" The options were 5% of a year's profit (recommended), 1% of annual revenue, or no threshold and stop.\n  Alex chose \"一年利润的 5% (Recommended)\", whose stated terms were:\n  - \"单笔未签承诺约达到公司一年利润的 5% 才单独开'会不会签'（亏损公司另议）\";\n  - \"金额不知道的，比如俄亥俄，仍按文章描述定性判断\";\n  - \"公司最近一年利润作为固定资料交给小步骤\".\n- **Decided.** Under D388, a single unsigned obligation is large enough for its own signing question when its stated amount is about 5%\n  or more of the company's most recent annual profit. An obligation whose amount is not stated is judged qualitatively from what the\n  item states. The company's most recent annual profit is supplied to the step as fixed input, with its source. A loss-making company\n  is not covered and is decided when one arises.\n- **Why.** In the focused D388 call, the same $2bn stake opened in 0 of 3 draws under one wording and 3 of 3 under another, and a\n  $2.5–3bn stake opened in 6 of 6, even when compared with stated revenue (round log §§54–55). The standard's \"large enough to change\"\n  (D248 boundary 6) had no anchor the model applied consistently. The 5% line agrees with every known verdict:\n  - small: about $2bn, $2.5–3bn, Intel's $5bn;\n  - open: Hugging Face at $12.9bn.\n- **Scope.** It applies to the focused D388 step under test. It enters the clean-arch PRD only if that step is adopted. The frozen\n  extraction standard and gold are unchanged (AGENTS §7.1).\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '271,326p' docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html\"","aggregated_output":"<h2 id=\"types\"><span class=\"num\">3</span>问题的五类：账本的几大类型</h2>\n<p>开题理由是 D184 定的四类，D236 把主驱动量扩到产品节点，所以写成五类。判两件事，互不顶替：这是谁的问题（标的还是主题）；为什么值得开（开题理由）。</p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap wide\"><table>\n<thead><tr><th>类</th><th>开题理由</th><th>标的或主题</th><th>问什么</th><th>量还是事件</th><th>期间和到期</th><th>核对材料 <code>settled_by</code></th><th>出处</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td class=\"nowrap\"><b>A</b> 主驱动量</td><td><code>main_driver</code></td><td>标的</td><td>承载公司价值的那个年度量，不管公司指不指引：撑起业务的分部收入、毛利率、资本开支；跨行业如银行的净利息收入、零售商的同店销售、公用事业的费率基数、航空公司的燃油成本（当它是争论焦点时）。不是每一行报表数</td><td>量，五档</td><td>公司财年的今年或明年；到期日是这个数的发布日</td><td>公布这个数的公开材料，通常是年报</td><td>D184：<code>settled_by</code> 是 \"the public material that resolves it\"；PRD 06 梯子第 5 条</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"nowrap\"><b>B</b> 主产品节点</td><td><code>main_driver</code></td><td>标的</td><td>承载公司价值的那一代产品哪天走到能带来收入的那一步（通常是开始出货）；发布、送样是它的证据，只有会分别下注的里程碑（新药的三期数据和获批）各一题<span class=\"src\">D248 第 3 条</span></td><td>事件，五档，或是非两档<span class=\"src\">PRD 06 梯子第 1 条</span></td><td>能判出结果的那天</td><td>公司公告、发货确认</td><td>D236</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"nowrap\"><b>C</b> 约束性义务</td><td><code>binding_obligation</code></td><td>标的</td><td>公司以自己名义承担的：为别人的债务、租约或收入担保或提供信用支持；借钱给别人；承诺购买（向别人买产能或服务也算）；为客户的产能或收入兜底；或写明规模、尚未完成的入股或收购<span class=\"src\">D236；收购按 D243 第 7 条</span>。规模要大到能改变公司的收入、利润、现金或信用风险才开；够不上的单笔入股、收购、租约、授信不开题，陈述留不留照第 5 节判<span class=\"src\">D248 第 6 条</span>。不算：自己借钱、自己的租约、已完成或没写规模的投资。D239 选定的 role-v29 原文：\"Its own borrowing, its own leases and a completed or unsized investment are not obligations\"；D238 的记录写作 \"the company's own borrowing and leases and a completed or unsized stake do not\"</td><td>还没签：是非两档。已经承担（一笔或一个计划）：金额，五档</td><td>检查日最多在文章后 18 个月<span class=\"src\">D185</span>；已承担的按下一份年报</td><td>签约公告、年报承诺附注</td><td>D184、D185、D210、D236、D238、D243</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"nowrap\"><b>D</b> 共同量</td><td><code>shared_quantity</code><span class=\"src\">D191、D243 第 2 条</span>；现行提示词和代码还叫 <code>industry_aggregate</code>，按这一页改</td><td>主题</td><td>任何一家公司之外、好几家都会受它影响的量或价格：几家公司的合计（云厂商资本开支）、价格（内存合约价、油价）、利率。同一总量的另一种人群、另一种说法是这个量的证据</td><td>量，五档</td><td>自然年的今年或明年。同一个量、同一年只有一个问题，由代码按\"主题＋量＋期间\"判<span class=\"src\">D197</span>；量的类别是 <code>other</code> 的不算</td><td>几家公司年报、统计发布、官方决定</td><td>D184、D191、D197、D243；PRD 06</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"nowrap\"><b>E</b> 政策阶段</td><td><code>policy_stage</code></td><td>问的是一家公司的收入、利润、份额或产品进度，算标的，即使由政策驱动；问的是世界上的事（许可制度、利率、合计支出），算主题。D184 采纳的 role-v12 原文：\"A question about a company's revenue, profit, share or product progress is an asset thesis; put its ticker in object, even when policy or macroeconomics drives it\"</td><td>一个政策或监管过程到了哪一步，写明谁说了算</td><td>事件，五档或两档</td><td>能判出那一步的那天。文章没写日期的待决监管事项，用本财年末（role-v12 原文：\"A pending regulatory decision may lack a date; use the current fiscal year-end as its due date\"）；这个日期是研究员定的检查日，要标明<span class=\"src\">评审 §1 第 1 条</span></td><td>官方决定、公报</td><td>D184</td></tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n<p>例子（跨行业）：</p>\n<ul>\n<li><b>A：</b>NVIDIA FY2027 数据中心收入；一家地区银行 FY2026 净利息收入；一家公用事业公司 2027 年费率基数。</li>\n<li><b>B：</b>下一代机架系统能否在 2027 年底前开始出货；一家车企的新平台能否在 2026 年内开始交付。</li>\n<li><b>C：</b>NVIDIA 为云客户产能兜底的义务在 FY2027 年报达到多少；一家保险公司是否在 2027 年中前为合资公司 5 亿美元债务签署担保。</li>\n<li><b>D：</b>五家最大云厂商 2026 年合计资本开支；2027 年 DRAM 合约价相对 2026 年的变化、美联储 2026 年最后一次会议后的利率上限。</li>\n<li><b>E：</b>中国是否在 2027-01-31 前正式批准本国公司进口 H200；美国是否在某日前对某类芯片实行出口许可。这两题问的是许可这件世界上的事，所以是主题，role-v12 原文的例子就是 \"licensing\"。一个监管决定对一家公司收入或产品进度的影响，问成那家公司的量或产品节点时，是标的问题（同一句原文）。</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>五类之外的东西去哪</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><b>七类驱动不是问题类型。</b>它们是一条陈述为什么重要的理由，用来判分量和归档。D208 设计的\"每家公司种下的驱动问题\"由分析员开始覆盖时写好，不从文章里开；还没建。</li>\n<li><b>别家公司自己的量</b>（对手的份额、客户的资本开支）：D187 定了\"任何公司自己的量是那家公司的问题，私营公司也算\"，但还没实现，要先在覆盖名单里加私营公司这一类。D155 定了\"公司清单可以作为初始参考，但清单外不能忽略\"。现行代码在匹配时跳过名单外的对象<span class=\"src\">PRD 06 Step 4</span>。所以抽取照常可以提这样的问题，它要过第 4 节的测试；名单外的现在会被匹配跳过，这不算抽取错。</li>\n<li><b>宏观量</b>（利率、通胀）：按 D 类共同量开题<span class=\"src\">D243 第 2 条</span>。只来自一篇纯宏观文章时，只有主题在名单上才开<span class=\"src\">D191 第 3 条</span>。宏观对每家公司的正负，在判断那家公司时读主题块决定<span class=\"src\">D191 第 1 条、D195</span>。</li>\n<li><b>开题理由是封闭的</b><span class=\"src\">D184</span>：一件事属不属于五类之一，按上表逐条看，比如一个监管决定看它是不是 E 类。哪一类都不属于的不开；它是不是证据、挂到哪，照第 5 节和归档规则。</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>问题怎么写：PRD 06 的梯子规则，不重写</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>一个问题只问一个量的一个期间，或一件事；能各自朝相反方向走、而且分析员会分别下注的部分要分开<span class=\"src\">PRD 06 梯子第 3 条；\"分别下注\"是 D248 加的，PRD 06 签字后更新</span>，分开的每一题都要过第 4 节的测试。</li>\n<li>写成问句，不写成断言<span class=\"src\">PRD 06 Rationale</span>。</li>\n<li>结果档可核对、不重叠、不留缝，到期恰好一档成立；中间一档写明和什么比；\"小幅\"\"部分\"这种不能核对的说法不用，部分状态写成单独一档<span class=\"src\">PRD 06 梯子第 2 条</span>。标的问题的档描述业务结果；主题问题的档只写结局，不写好坏<span class=\"src\">PRD 06、D186</span>。</li>\n<li>到期日：量是它的发布日；事件是能判出结果的那天。公司的量用公司财年，别的用自然年，只开今年和明年<span class=\"src\">PRD 06 梯子第 5 条；约束性义务例外，D185</span>。</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2 id=\"opening\"><span class=\"num\">4</span>开题标准</h2>\n<blockquote><p><b>一个问题值得单独追，要同时满足三件事：它的答案可能改变仓位；能在一个日期用公开材料判出落在哪一档；库里没有问题在问同一件事。</b>开多少个是判断的结果，不是目标<span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §6；评审 §1</span>。</p>\n<p>颗粒度按一个高端对冲基金分析员：只有会单独下注的大事开题，鸡毛蒜皮不开题（它的陈述留不留照第 5 节判）；同一个赌注的几种说法是一题，截止日、里程碑、财年和日历年各按本节\"同一题、续期，还是另一题\"里的那一条判<span class=\"src\">D248</span>。</p>\n<p>另有一条前提：新问题要有独立的投资判断；一个新产品、一个新数字、一个更窄的范围，单凭这些不开<span class=\"src\">D201</span>。</p></blockquote>\n\n<h3>四个测试<span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §6</span></h3>\n<ol class=\"steps\">\n<li><b>值得追</b>写得出\"这个结果会改变哪项收入、利润、现金或信用风险、竞争位置\"吗？写不出就留作证据，不开题。\"数字很大\"不算理由。单笔交易、产品、项目，规模够不上改变公司的收入、利润、现金或信用风险的，不开题，陈述留不留照第 5 节判<span class=\"src\">D248 第 6 条：问的就是小交易、小产品</span>；这一测试的其余理由（包括竞争位置）不变。</li>\n<li><b>独立意义</b>能写出两个情景吗：其他问题的答案不变，只有这一题相反，而对业务的判断确实不同？写不出就优先作为证据<span class=\"src\">评审 §1 第 3、8 条</span>。评审里的一个判例：NVIDIA FY2027 总收入题判为数据中心收入题的证据，理由是\"该段明确说主要增长来自数据中心，未提出独立的其他业务争论\"。这是对那一段材料的判断，别的材料要逐个判。</li>\n<li><b>能核对</b>有一个日期和一份公开材料能把答案放进事先固定的档吗？没有就重写问题。到期没有材料记\"未能判定\"，不算错。</li>\n<li><b>不是重复</b>和已有问题比，只是预测值、措辞、来源、方向或同一总量的另一种口径不同，最终核对的是同一个结果吗？是就是同一题。抽取看不到库<span class=\"src\">D211</span>，这一条在抽取时只对同一篇文章里提出的几个问题判；和库里的比由匹配做。</li>\n</ol>\n<p>另外三条写法检查<span class=\"src\">评审 §1 第 1、5、6 条</span>。没过的问题不能照原样开，要重写；重写不了就不开，材料作证据。</p>\n<ul>\n<li><b>原文支持：</b>主体、量或事件、时间依据都能在原文找到。原文没给日期、而规则允许研究员定检查日的，用那个日期并标明：没写日期的待决监管事项用本财年末（第 3 节 E 类）；还没签的约束性义务用文章后 18 个月以内能核对签约的那天<span class=\"src\">D185、D210</span>。不把\"拟议\"\"预计\"写成\"已签\"\"已完成\"。</li>\n<li><b>口径完整：</b>算谁、不算谁、算什么写清楚；支出、融资、担保、订单、收入不混。</li>\n<li><b>时间正确：</b>原文支持这个期间，不把几年的平均写成今年。</li>\n</ul>\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'diff -u clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c8-schema.json clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c18-schema.json'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'diff -u clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c8-schema.json clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c18-schema.json'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c18-system.txt | sed -n '95,132p'; nl -ba clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c18-closing.txt | tail -5\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c18-system.txt | sed -n '95,132p'; nl -ba clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c18-closing.txt | tail -5\"","aggregated_output":"    95\t- binding_obligation: an obligation the company takes on in its own name, large enough to change its revenue, profit, cash or credit\n    96\t  risk: guaranteeing, backing or giving credit support for another party's debt, lease, revenue or capacity, lending to it,\n    97\t  committing to buy capacity or services, or a sized stake or acquisition not yet completed. One already undertaken is tracked by its\n    98\t  amount at the next annual report; one not yet signed by whether it is signed by a check date within 18 months of the item (\"how much will the\n    99\t  utility have guaranteed for its project companies' loans at its next annual report?\"; \"will the retailer sign a guarantee for its\n   100\t  franchisees' leases, large enough to change its credit risk, by the check date?\"). Its own borrowing or leases and a completed\n   101\t  or unsized investment are not obligations. An unsigned single deal large enough on its own to change those keeps its own signing thesis\n   102\t  even when a thesis on the total of its kind is open, since whether it is signed can move apart from the total; a deal an open thesis\n   103\t  already tracks, a small one, or one signed under a programme tracked by its amount is evidence for the open thesis (\"whether an\n   104\t  airline signs one large aircraft order, beside the thesis on its total purchase commitments\"; \"one more small supplier prepayment\n   105\t  under a programme already tracked by its amount\").\n   106\t- shared_quantity: a quantity or price outside any one company that several companies depend on, for this or next calendar year:\n   107\t  several companies' combined output or spending, a contract price, an interest rate (\"the largest container lines' combined capacity\n   108\t  added in 2026\"; \"next year's average contract price of a raw material\"). Another population or wording of the same aggregate is\n   109\t  evidence for it.\n   110\t- policy_stage: the step a policy or regulatory process reaches, naming who decides (\"will the regulator approve the drug for a second\n   111\t  indication?\"; \"will the government require licences for the product's exports by a date?\").\n   112\t\n   113\t- Open only matters an analyst would bet on separately; small matters open no thesis and their statements are kept as evidence. A\n   114\t  customer's deployment plan is evidence for the company's demand and product theses, unless it changes the company's own cash or\n   115\t  credit risk, which is judged as an obligation.\n   116\t- Give the date the item supports. When it gives none, use the date the reason fixes and say how it was set: an obligation already\n   117\t  undertaken, its next annual report; an unsigned obligation, a check date within 18 months of the item; a pending regulatory\n   118\t  decision, the current fiscal year-end. A shared quantity takes its release date and a product event the date its outcome can be\n   119\t  checked, only when the item supports one. A question no date can settle is rewritten or not opened.\n   120\t- Do not open a thesis about: an executive appointment or organisational change; the company's own borrowing or leases as an\n   121\t  obligation; a buyback authorisation or dividend declaration; a financial measure's level, growth, margin or guidance for any period,\n   122\t  on its own; an undated moat or strategy; a feature, content or software update, price point, regional service or variant of a\n   123\t  product already on sale; another estimate, source or wording of what an open thesis tracks; an annual quantity after next year (an\n   124\t  obligation excepted); shareholder votes, bylaws or routine litigation procedure. Their statements are evidence for the theses they\n   125\t  inform, or left unlinked.\n   126\t- Before proposing a new thesis, name its reason (opens_as), the public material that will settle it (settled_by), and the closest\n   127\t  open thesis with why an analyst would bet on the two separately because their answers can move apart; with no open thesis, say so.\n   128\t  If the two cannot move apart, link the evidence to every open thesis it informs instead.\n   129\t\n   130\tCounterexamples:\n   131\t\n   132\t- \"The company's outlook is interesting\" or \"the industry may change\" is too vague: it names no outcome later evidence can inform.\n    12\tA report and another party's denial or confirmation of it are two items, each kept only if it passes the test above; an estimate stays apart from any valuation drawn from it, and the valuation is not kept; one party's statement keeps its own planned or rumoured details.\n    13\tReturn only the evidence items you keep.\n    14\tThen check the theses and links. A new thesis that asks the same underlying question, about the same subject and scope, as an open thesis or another new thesis is not proposed: link its evidence to that thesis. A new thesis needs at least one kept evidence item, and a vague or noisy topic with no outcome to watch is not proposed. Each kept evidence item links to every thesis it informs and to no thesis its own relevance says it does not inform.\n    15\tFor each new thesis, check its opens_as, settled_by, closest_open_thesis and why_a_separate_bet: drop the thesis if it fits none of the four reasons in section 3, if no public material will settle it on a date, if an open thesis exists and its answer cannot move apart from it, or if it falls under a 'do not open' item in section 3; then link its evidence to every open thesis it informs, or leave it without links.\n    16\tAn item whose only home would be a new thesis that is not a big matter is returned with empty links and kept without links; an item an open thesis covers is linked there, not left without links. Then read back each statement you return with empty links that states the company's own figures: return it only if a figure can change what an analyst expects of the company's revenue, profitability, funding or credit risk, or competitive position; for example, a cash-rich company's balance or cash flow that the item ties to nothing usually cannot; return only what passes.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"agent_message","text":"The new sentence captures Alex’s decision for a major unsigned deal beside a question about the total, but it is **too broad in two places**. It treats the ability to move separately as a reason to open without expressly requiring a separate investment judgment, and it says some deals are evidence for an open question without limiting that statement to cases where the open question actually covers them.\n\nFor example, if a large aircraft order is already the subject of an open “will it be signed?” question, the new sentence first appears to say it keeps its own question, then says a deal already tracked is evidence. The rest of the request rejects the duplicate, but the new sentence itself gives the model mixed signals.\n\nI ran the diffs: [c18’s system text](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c18-system.txt:101) adds one sentence; the closing check is unchanged. The c8 and c18 schemas are also identical.\n\nThe sentence has several distinct instructions, so I assessed each part:\n\n| Changed words | Verdict | Basis |\n|---|---|---|\n| “An unsigned single deal large enough on its own to change those keeps its own signing thesis even when a thesis on the total of its kind is open” | **Keeps wider** | [D388](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:4172) requires a material unsigned obligation **that merits a separate investment judgment**. The signed standard requires answers that “能分开走、而且分析员会分别下注” ([§4](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:343)). The new clause explicitly states size but leaves that separate-judgment condition to other sentences. It also does not qualify its direction for a signing question already open. |\n| “since whether it is signed can move apart from the total” | **Keeps wider** | Separate movement is necessary under §4, but §4 also asks whether the analyst would bet separately. Here “since” presents separation as the reason, rather than a case-specific test. A total can have other contributors, but that alone does not establish a separate investment judgment. |\n| “a deal an open thesis already tracks … is evidence for the open thesis” | **Consistent**, subject to the ambiguity above | The standard says “同一个结果能判掉两题，就是同一题” and merges the candidate into the open question ([§4](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:343)). This clause conflicts in scope with the earlier unconditional “keeps its own signing thesis” when the *same deal’s signing* is already tracked. |\n| “a small one … is evidence for the open thesis” | **Keeps wider** | D388 says a small unsigned obligation stays evidence **for the total** in the case it addresses. The standard says a small deal does not open a question and whether to keep its statement is judged separately: “陈述留不留照第 5 节判” ([§3](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:278)). “The open thesis” is not necessarily a covering total; the wording also skips the separate decision about whether the statement is worth keeping. |\n| “one signed under a programme tracked by its amount is evidence for the open thesis” | **Consistent** in D388’s covered case | D388 says a deal already signed under a plan tracked by amount stays evidence for the total. The standard likewise says a transaction that is part of a plan tracked by amount is merged into it ([§4](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:354)). It should not be read as ruling out a *different*, independently important question the same statement informs. |\n\n[D389](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:4185) adds a specific size test for the focused step under test: approximately 5% of the latest annual profit when the amount is stated; qualitative judgment when it is not; and a sourced annual-profit input. The candidate sentence and unchanged schema do not express that threshold or input. Therefore, **if c18 is intended to implement D389, it keeps the size decision wider and less specified**. D389 expressly limits its scope to the focused step and leaves the frozen standard unchanged; I cannot infer from these files alone that c18 has adopted that scoped decision.\n\n1. **Other request sentences.** The most direct tension is between “keeps its own signing thesis” and both “a deal an open thesis already tracks” and the closing check’s instruction not to propose the same underlying question. “Can move apart” also risks weakening “an analyst would bet on separately”: the former is not sufficient by itself. There is no necessary contradiction with “another estimate, source or wording” when the deal’s signing and the total are genuinely different outcomes; there is one if the open question already asks whether that deal will be signed. Nor does the sentence expressly contradict the 18-month date rule, but the aircraft example omits a check date and could make an incomplete question look sufficient. The existing date instruction still applies.\n\n   The instruction to link evidence to every question it informs remains in both the system text and closing check. The added sentence does **not** explicitly say to stop linking a major deal to the total, but “keeps its own signing thesis” may focus the model on the new question without reminding it that the same statement can also inform the total.\n\n2. **Examples.** Neither example names a covered company, a named product, or a number. They use airline and supplier settings, but their underlying distinction can apply across industries. The aircraft-order example illustrates D388 only if the order is independently important and an existing question does not already track that signing; it does not state either condition or a check date. The small prepayment example is consistent with D388 when it is part of the programme and informs its tracked total; it does not establish whether the statement itself passes the evidence test. Both can be represented in the schema: the first through a new question, date, settlement material and links; the second through an existing-question link. The examples themselves are abbreviated, not complete schema outputs.\n\n3. **Possible effects.** These are risks from the wording, not observed model behavior:\n\n   - **Duplicate deal question:** “keeps its own signing thesis even when” can be read as an instruction to open despite an already-open question about that same signing. The later “already tracks” clause and closing check push against it.\n   - **Small-deal signing question:** “large enough on its own to change those” is qualitative and does not encode D389’s scoped threshold. A model could judge a deal large under that phrase even where D389’s stated-amount test would not. The explicit “a small one” and “small matters open no thesis” otherwise tell it not to open small deals.\n   - **Missing link to the total:** “keeps its own signing thesis” names the separate question but does not explicitly say that the deal can inform **both** questions. The general link-all instructions do say so.\n   - **Suppressed openings:** “a deal an open thesis already tracks” could be read as coverage of the deal as a whole, even when a distinct outcome deserves separate tracking. “One signed under a programme … is evidence” could similarly be overread as excluding every other independently important question about that deal. The general separate-outcome rule works against that reading.\n\nThis was a read-only audit of the text; I did not run model calls or change files.\n\n"}}
